Awesome. The **Pagination "Phantom Row" Bug** is one of the most common silent data killers in enterprise dashboards.
### Why this happens
When Oracle (or any SQL database) runs an ORDER BY CREATED_AT DESC query, it sorts the rows by time. But if an automated system inserts 10 batches in the exact same second, they all have the *exact same timestamp*.
When your React frontend asks for "Page 1 (rows 1-10)", Oracle grabs 10 rows. When it asks for "Page 2 (rows 11-20)", Oracle recalculates the sort. Because the timestamps are identical, Oracle doesn't guarantee the order of the tie. It might shuffle them, causing some rows from Page 1 to appear again on Page 2, while completely skipping others. Users will report that data is "missing."
### The Fix
We simply add a unique tie-breaker to the ORDER BY clause. Since BATCH_ID is always unique, we use that.
Open **VoucherQueryService.java**, find the getAllRequestsSummary method (around line 95), and update the dataSql string:
**Change this:**
```sql
        ORDER BY p.CREATED_AT DESC
        OFFSET ? ROWS FETCH NEXT ? ROWS ONLY

```
**To this:**
```sql
        -- Added p.BATCH_ID DESC as the deterministic tie-breaker
        ORDER BY p.CREATED_AT DESC, p.BATCH_ID DESC
        OFFSET ? ROWS FETCH NEXT ? ROWS ONLY

```
Here is exactly how that block should look in your code:
